// KeyedPointA of ../KeyedPointA.idl for fastddsgen. `@must_understand` on
// the key is what XTypes 1.3 §7.2.2.4.4.4.8 makes implicit ("key members
// shall always have their 'must understand' attribute set to true").
// ZeroDDS and Cyclone DDS set IS_MUST_UNDERSTAND on a key member without
// it; the Fast DDS 3.6.1 type support fastddsgen generates does not
// (measured on the Linux test host: its TypeLookup reply carries member flags 0x0021,
// TRY_CONSTRUCT1 | IS_KEY), so the two minimal TypeObjects differ in that
// one flag, their hashes differ, and the reader does not match a ZeroDDS
// writer that announces its TypeInformation. Written out, the flag gives
// both the TypeObject the specification asks for.
@final
struct KeyedPointA {
    @key @must_understand long id;
    long value;
};
